Dialogue: 0,00:00:00.00,00:00:01.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi guys!
Dialogue: 0,00:00:02.16,00:00:03.80,Default,,0,0,0,,I am Pranay
Dialogue: 0,00:00:03.80,00:00:06.36,Default,,0,0,0,,We are going to talk about
Dialogue: 0,00:00:06.60,00:00:08.56,Default,,0,0,0,,how to increase your bench press from
Dialogue: 0,00:00:08.56,00:00:10.92,Default,,0,0,0,,70 kgs to 100 kg-plus
Dialogue: 0,00:00:11.68,00:00:14.28,Default,,0,0,0,,that's fine with me. I'm kidding
Dialogue: 0,00:00:14.96,00:00:17.04,Default,,0,0,0,,We're going to talk about Benchmarks
Dialogue: 0,00:00:17.04,00:00:18.60,Default,,0,0,0,,like the life cycle of a benchmark
Dialogue: 0,00:00:18.60,00:00:21.36,Default,,0,0,0,,and what happens when a benchmark is
Dialogue: 0,00:00:21.36,00:00:25.04,Default,,0,0,0,,released and how people use it? How
Dialogue: 0,00:00:25.04,00:00:27.20,Default,,0,0,0,,do people to optimise for it?
Dialogue: 0,00:00:28.08,00:00:29.36,Default,,0,0,0,,so yeah
Dialogue: 0,00:00:30.28,00:00:32.88,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the second time that I'm doing this. So, the first time i
Dialogue: 0,00:00:32.88,00:00:35.16,Default,,0,0,0,,try to sell my product. So, this time
Dialogue: 0,00:00:35.16,00:00:37.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going to try to
Dialogue: 0,00:00:38.12,00:00:40.16,Default,,0,0,0,,teach you something which you can only
Dialogue: 0,00:00:40.32,00:00:43.12,Default,,0,0,0,,take away from i know this is
Dialogue: 0,00:00:43.12,00:00:46.16,Default,,0,0,0,,And, this is something that is locked usually in
Dialogue: 0,00:00:46.56,00:00:48.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Frontier AI Labs
Dialogue: 0,00:00:48.28,00:00:51.00,Default,,0,0,0,,which is usually not accessible
Dialogue: 0,00:00:53.24,00:00:58.12,Default,,0,0,0,,When there is a Benchmark that is released,
Dialogue: 0,00:00:58.12,00:00:59.24,Default,,0,0,0,,what happens is people
Dialogue: 0,00:00:59.24,00:01:00.84,Default,,0,0,0,,first look at the types of tasks
Dialogue: 0,00:01:00.84,00:01:04.16,Default,,0,0,0,,that each Benchmark has.
Dialogue: 0,00:01:04.40,00:01:06.92,Default,,0,0,0,,And, then they realize:
Dialogue: 0,00:01:06.92,00:01:10.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, does this task look like it's important to me?
Dialogue: 0,00:01:10.56,00:01:14.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's say - I am a Software Engineer. Or a Data Scientist
Dialogue: 0,00:01:14.00,00:01:18.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it important for me or for the Agent to be able to
Dialogue: 0,00:01:18.72,00:01:23.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's say- write python script or let's say write Model Architecture and stuff like that?
Dialogue: 0,00:01:24.20,00:01:27.00,Default,,0,0,0,,So, eventually what happens is
Dialogue: 0,00:01:27.00,00:01:29.72,Default,,0,0,0,,whenever a very good Benchmark comes out,
Dialogue: 0,00:01:30.60,00:01:35.84,Default,,0,0,0,,then, usually even a 2 points improvement on a benchmark. Like:
Dialogue: 0,00:01:35.84,00:01:41.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's say GPT 5.5 is 80% and Fable, I think is reported at 82%
Dialogue: 0,00:01:42.32,00:01:46.76,Default,,0,0,0,,And, with a 2% difference, you can raise like hundred Million
Dialogue: 0,00:01:46.76,00:01:48.16,Default,,0,0,0,,or something like that
Dialogue: 0,00:01:48.72,00:01:51.80,Default,,0,0,0,,So, what exactly is Benchmaxxxing?
Dialogue: 0,00:01:51.84,00:01:54.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Benchmaxxxing is like -
Dialogue: 0,00:01:54.20,00:01:57.20,Default,,0,0,0,,When there is a set of tasks and you have to increase
Dialogue: 0,00:01:57.52,00:02:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,your performance on that task, or on those tasks.
Dialogue: 0,00:02:00.08,00:02:03.32,Default,,0,0,0,,So, there are a bunch of variables
Dialogue: 0,00:02:03.32,00:02:04.72,Default,,0,0,0,,that you can tune.
Dialogue: 0,00:02:04.72,00:02:07.08,Default,,0,0,0,,The Model is not the only variable,
Dialogue: 0,00:02:07.08,00:02:12.36,Default,,0,0,0,,the Harness, the Verification, the Tests- everything is part of that.
Dialogue: 0,00:02:12.36,00:02:15.64,Default,,0,0,0,,So, this is specifically
Dialogue: 0,00:02:15.64,00:02:20.00,Default,,0,0,0,,for Coding and Math Benchmarks - which are verifiable
Dialogue: 0,00:02:20.00,00:02:21.56,Default,,0,0,0,,in nature
Dialogue: 0,00:02:21.56,00:02:24.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Very briefly we are going to talk about the part
Dialogue: 0,00:02:24.28,00:02:26.12,Default,,0,0,0,,that i'm working on
Dialogue: 0,00:02:26.12,00:02:28.24,Default,,0,0,0,,my project which is basically on the
Dialogue: 0,00:02:28.24,00:02:31.52,Default,,0,0,0,,EVM Bench
Dialogue: 0,00:02:31.52,00:02:34.24,Default,,0,0,0,,like is based on smart contracts and
Dialogue: 0,00:02:34.24,00:02:36.80,Default,,0,0,0,,these smart contracts are basically deployed in
Dialogue: 0,00:02:37.12,00:02:41.96,Default,,0,0,0,,De-Fi, Social, Lending, AMMs and lot
Dialogue: 0,00:02:41.96,00:02:43.40,Default,,0,0,0,,of other applications. Like, these are called
Dialogue: 0,00:02:43.40,00:02:46.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Decentralised Applications
Dialogue: 0,00:02:46.40,00:02:51.12,Default,,0,0,0,,And, Smart Contracts- Ones who write them and they are deployed onto the BlockChain,
Dialogue: 0,00:02:51.12,00:02:54.72,Default,,0,0,0,,you can't change them. It's immutable code.
Dialogue: 0,00:02:55.68,00:02:58.48,Default,,0,0,0,,This EVM Bench - is basically a set of 120 tasks
Dialogue: 0,00:02:58.92,00:03:02.16,Default,,0,0,0,,across 40 different smart contracts.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:03.36,00:03:07.36,Default,,0,0,0,,And they're basically like a frontier
Dialogue: 0,00:03:07.36,00:03:10.16,Default,,0,0,0,,EVAL Benchmark release by OpenAI
Dialogue: 0,00:03:11.00,00:03:14.52,Default,,0,0,0,,And, what they are trying to figure out
Dialogue: 0,00:03:14.52,00:03:17.24,Default,,0,0,0,,is that why do models don't perform well?
Dialogue: 0,00:03:17.36,00:03:19.68,Default,,0,0,0,,We will see that in the
Dialogue: 0,00:03:19.68,00:03:21.44,Default,,0,0,0,,next few slides.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:21.44,00:03:23.60,Default,,0,0,0,,One thing I wanted to mention like I want to highlight here
Dialogue: 0,00:03:23.60,00:03:25.40,Default,,0,0,0,,is a Docker Local Chain.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:26.16,00:03:29.00,Default,,0,0,0,,What you'll see is that mostly in Coding Benchmarks,
Dialogue: 0,00:03:29.00,00:03:30.96,Default,,0,0,0,,what happens is
Dialogue: 0,00:03:30.96,00:03:33.00,Default,,0,0,0,,the structure is usually the same.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:33.00,00:03:35.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Like, there is always a separate environment.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:35.04,00:03:37.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Like, the Docker part is the grader.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:38.64,00:03:40.76,Default,,0,0,0,,and the evaluation and the execution all of it
Dialogue: 0,00:03:40.76,00:03:43.64,Default,,0,0,0,,happens in the Docker Container,
Dialogue: 0,00:03:44.28,00:03:46.16,Default,,0,0,0,,which is the environment.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:47.28,00:03:49.56,Default,,0,0,0,,So, then, while I was working on it
Dialogue: 0,00:03:49.80,00:03:52.24,Default,,0,0,0,,my setup was basically GPT 5.4
Dialogue: 0,00:03:52.24,00:03:55.04,Default,,0,0,0,,and Codex, and OpenCode
Dialogue: 0,00:03:55.04,00:03:57.48,Default,,0,0,0,,and I ran it across all of the EVM Bench tasks.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:57.48,00:03:59.96,Default,,0,0,0,,What i found out was that -
Dialogue: 0,00:04:00.20,00:04:02.96,Default,,0,0,0,,the results are pathetic!
Dialogue: 0,00:04:02.96,00:04:04.88,Default,,0,0,0,,And, Frontier Models are NOT that good!
Dialogue: 0,00:04:04.88,00:04:06.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanted to run this for Opus, but
Dialogue: 0,00:04:06.68,00:04:06.96,Default,,0,0,0,,but
Dialogue: 0,00:04:07.04,00:04:09.32,Default,,0,0,0,,every single task here takes
Dialogue: 0,00:04:09.32,00:04:11.96,Default,,0,0,0,,about two hundred to three hundred tool calls
Dialogue: 0,00:04:12.08,00:04:14.12,Default,,0,0,0,,not tool calls - API calls
Dialogue: 0,00:04:14.64,00:04:17.04,Default,,0,0,0,,And, it gets very expensive and they run for
Dialogue: 0,00:04:17.04,00:04:20.12,Default,,0,0,0,,one and a half, two hours. Each!
Dialogue: 0,00:04:20.12,00:04:21.76,Default,,0,0,0,,So, these would run overnight and
Dialogue: 0,00:04:22.64,00:04:24.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to Aditya (Adi)!
Dialogue: 0,00:04:24.88,00:04:29.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I've spent up more than like, two thousand dollars worth of
Dialogue: 0,00:04:29.28,00:04:30.88,Default,,0,0,0,,his compute on Azure credits.
Dialogue: 0,00:04:31.12,00:04:32.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks Adi! :)
Dialogue: 0,00:04:32.60,00:04:34.36,Default,,0,0,0,,So, while i was trying
Dialogue: 0,00:04:34.36,00:04:35.04,Default,,0,0,0,,to figure out
Dialogue: 0,00:04:36.04,00:04:38.68,Default,,0,0,0,,how do I improve performance on EVM Bench,
Dialogue: 0,00:04:38.68,00:04:40.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I was trying to dive deeper
Dialogue: 0,00:04:40.36,00:04:42.08,Default,,0,0,0,,into it. So, frmo all of the traces that
Dialogue: 0,00:04:42.08,00:04:44.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I had this is what i found out:
Dialogue: 0,00:04:45.72,00:04:48.68,Default,,0,0,0,,This is basically the split - like the
Dialogue: 0,00:04:48.72,00:04:51.60,Default,,0,0,0,,distribution of what kind of tools does
Dialogue: 0,00:04:51.60,00:04:53.64,Default,,0,0,0,,the Agent call.
Dialogue: 0,00:04:54.28,00:04:56.60,Default,,0,0,0,,You can go to this QR code,
Dialogue: 0,00:04:56.60,00:04:58.92,Default,,0,0,0,,and look at like more insights there.
Dialogue: 0,00:04:58.92,00:05:01.12,Default,,0,0,0,,If you're trying to
Dialogue: 0,00:05:01.12,00:05:03.44,Default,,0,0,0,,increase your performance on some kind of a Coding Benchmark,
Dialogue: 0,00:05:03.44,00:05:06.96,Default,,0,0,0,,then these insights will definitely help you. So, you can check them out.
Dialogue: 0,00:05:06.96,00:05:09.84,Default,,0,0,0,,While i was trying to understand
Dialogue: 0,00:05:09.84,00:05:12.40,Default,,0,0,0,,the distribution here, I was looking at
Dialogue: 0,00:05:12.68,00:05:13.44,Default,,0,0,0,,other benchmarks
Dialogue: 0,00:05:14.16,00:05:16.00,Default,,0,0,0,,which also had the same structure
Dialogue: 0,00:05:16.04,00:05:18.08,Default,,0,0,0,,So, a very common one is - SWE Bench
Dialogue: 0,00:05:18.08,00:05:20.36,Default,,0,0,0,,and I was looking through SWE Bench
Dialogue: 0,00:05:20.36,00:05:22.40,Default,,0,0,0,,and then I found out this article
Dialogue: 0,00:05:22.40,00:05:24.88,Default,,0,0,0,,by OpenAI. And what it said is that -
Dialogue: 0,00:05:24.88,00:05:27.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Performance on SWE Bench - it does not tell you
Dialogue: 0,00:05:27.88,00:05:32.16,Default,,0,0,0,,about the Frontier capabilities of models. And, why is that?
Dialogue: 0,00:05:32.16,00:05:34.28,Default,,0,0,0,,That's simply because number of
Dialogue: 0,00:05:34.32,00:05:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,tasks the and the type of
Dialogue: 0,00:05:35.96,00:05:38.68,Default,,0,0,0,,tasks that SWE Bench has,
Dialogue: 0,00:05:38.68,00:05:41.36,Default,,0,0,0,,there are too many similar tasks in the
Dialogue: 0,00:05:41.36,00:05:43.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Pre-Training and the Post-Training data. So,
Dialogue: 0,00:05:43.96,00:05:45.76,Default,,0,0,0,,they have been climbed upon so much
Dialogue: 0,00:05:45.76,00:05:47.88,Default,,0,0,0,,that you don't even need to
Dialogue: 0,00:05:47.88,00:05:49.48,Default,,0,0,0,,give them a question. Like, if you
Dialogue: 0,00:05:49.48,00:05:51.68,Default,,0,0,0,,just give them the Test
Dialogue: 0,00:05:51.72,00:05:53.80,Default,,0,0,0,,They will tell you the question and the answer.
Dialogue: 0,00:05:54.48,00:05:56.16,Default,,0,0,0,,which is very bad!
Dialogue: 0,00:05:56.16,00:05:58.40,Default,,0,0,0,,That's how they measured contamination in the Benchmark.
Dialogue: 0,00:05:58.88,00:06:01.16,Default,,0,0,0,,which is bad. They recommend SWE Bench Pro
Dialogue: 0,00:06:01.40,00:06:03.20,Default,,0,0,0,,which does not have these problems
Dialogue: 0,00:06:03.20,00:06:07.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I want you to think about it this way. If anything is verifyable,
Dialogue: 0,00:06:07.44,00:06:11.84,Default,,0,0,0,,and it is open source, people will be
Dialogue: 0,00:06:11.84,00:06:13.68,Default,,0,0,0,,able to figure out what
Dialogue: 0,00:06:14.64,00:06:16.92,Default,,0,0,0,,similar tasks to create so that you can
Dialogue: 0,00:06:16.92,00:06:18.40,Default,,0,0,0,,train on those new tasks
Dialogue: 0,00:06:18.48,00:06:20.80,Default,,0,0,0,,and then increase the capability on the
Dialogue: 0,00:06:20.80,00:06:22.52,Default,,0,0,0,,original task. While i was looking
Dialogue: 0,00:06:22.52,00:06:27.08,Default,,0,0,0,,through the distribution of SWE Bench- like how
Dialogue: 0,00:06:27.12,00:06:28.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Coding Models perform SWE Bench Tasks,
Dialogue: 0,00:06:30.64,00:06:33.80,Default,,0,0,0,,I found out that - this is the same
Dialogue: 0,00:06:34.24,00:06:38.04,Default,,0,0,0,,distribution across both EVM Bench Task and
Dialogue: 0,00:06:38.04,00:06:39.92,Default,,0,0,0,,SWE Bench Task, barring the on-chain state query
Dialogue: 0,00:06:39.92,00:06:41.76,Default,,0,0,0,,because SWE Bench does not
Dialogue: 0,00:06:41.76,00:06:43.40,Default,,0,0,0,,have on-chain state query.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:43.68,00:06:46.92,Default,,0,0,0,,This is only local to EVM Bench
Dialogue: 0,00:06:46.92,00:06:49.32,Default,,0,0,0,,But rest of it is basically the same. So,
Dialogue: 0,00:06:49.40,00:06:49.92,Default,,0,0,0,,remember
Dialogue: 0,00:06:50.28,00:06:52.52,Default,,0,0,0,,my objective here was to dive deep
Dialogue: 0,00:06:52.88,00:06:55.72,Default,,0,0,0,,and improve performance on EVM Bench
Dialogue: 0,00:06:55.72,00:06:57.68,Default,,0,0,0,,all I cared about. Okay? That is
Dialogue: 0,00:06:57.68,00:06:59.36,Default,,0,0,0,,not the right way by the way
Dialogue: 0,00:06:59.48,00:07:02.24,Default,,0,0,0,,that is all I care about
Dialogue: 0,00:07:02.24,00:07:04.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I think Paras helped me understand
Dialogue: 0,00:07:04.44,00:07:05.76,Default,,0,0,0,,why it is not the right way.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:05.76,00:07:06.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Because, improving
Dialogue: 0,00:07:07.68,00:07:09.20,Default,,0,0,0,,performance on a Benchmark does not
Dialogue: 0,00:07:09.20,00:07:11.72,Default,,0,0,0,,really prove that that is some
Dialogue: 0,00:07:11.72,00:07:14.16,Default,,0,0,0,,signs behind why those Benchmarks'
Dialogue: 0,00:07:14.16,00:07:16.92,Default,,0,0,0,,performance was improved. What it taught me was that that
Dialogue: 0,00:07:16.92,00:07:19.36,Default,,0,0,0,,If you can teach the model
Dialogue: 0,00:07:19.36,00:07:23.04,Default,,0,0,0,,the right type of localization, reproduction
Dialogue: 0,00:07:23.08,00:07:27.84,Default,,0,0,0,,editing and validation for a particular- let's say - Task type
Dialogue: 0,00:07:27.84,00:07:30.52,Default,,0,0,0,,then you don't really need to improve
Dialogue: 0,00:07:30.56,00:07:32.28,Default,,0,0,0,,general reasoning. It will just do. Like,
Dialogue: 0,00:07:32.28,00:07:33.96,Default,,0,0,0,,It will just be a parrot.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:34.36,00:07:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,And it will do very well on the benchmarks
Dialogue: 0,00:07:36.04,00:07:39.68,Default,,0,0,0,,but it will not explicitly show who reasoning.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:40.28,00:07:43.28,Default,,0,0,0,,A very simple example of it is this :
Dialogue: 0,00:07:43.28,00:07:46.48,Default,,0,0,0,,If you look at Chinese Models. Have you used- MiniMax?
Dialogue: 0,00:07:46.48,00:07:49.12,Default,,0,0,0,,M 2.5?
Dialogue: 0,00:07:49.12,00:07:50.76,Default,,0,0,0,,not M 2.7 because that was
Dialogue: 0,00:07:50.76,00:07:54.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Post-Trained on something different. But MiniMax M 2.5 - if you use it,
Dialogue: 0,00:07:54.48,00:07:56.64,Default,,0,0,0,,It's performing like 75%
Dialogue: 0,00:07:57.08,00:07:59.36,Default,,0,0,0,,on SWE Bench. And if you compare
Dialogue: 0,00:07:59.36,00:08:01.12,Default,,0,0,0,,it to OPUS of that time,
Dialogue: 0,00:08:03.36,00:08:06.32,Default,,0,0,0,,OPUS was at around 78-79%
Dialogue: 0,00:08:06.32,00:08:09.00,Default,,0,0,0,,and if you try to talk
Dialogue: 0,00:08:09.00,00:08:11.40,Default,,0,0,0,,to that Model, it would be pathetic.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:11.40,00:08:14.92,Default,,0,0,0,,It would not know. It would answer even normal questions with code,
Dialogue: 0,00:08:15.08,00:08:17.28,Default,,0,0,0,,which is not okay!
Dialogue: 0,00:08:17.28,00:08:19.64,Default,,0,0,0,,But, people would only use MiniMax M 2.5
Dialogue: 0,00:08:19.64,00:08:22.40,Default,,0,0,0,,specifically for code
Dialogue: 0,00:08:22.40,00:08:24.80,Default,,0,0,0,,in a coding harness. as a coding agent.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:27.92,00:08:28.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Now
Dialogue: 0,00:08:28.80,00:08:30.60,Default,,0,0,0,,2 points: This is by the way
Dialogue: 0,00:08:30.60,00:08:32.36,Default,,0,0,0,,the creator of the SWE Bench
Dialogue: 0,00:08:33.32,00:08:35.48,Default,,0,0,0,,so basically he was asking - do we
Dialogue: 0,00:08:36.24,00:08:39.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Benchmaxxx on SWE Bench or any
Dialogue: 0,00:08:39.72,00:08:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,kind of benchmark? Well, i think YES. Why? Because
Dialogue: 0,00:08:43.40,00:08:47.44,Default,,0,0,0,,think about- If the Chinese don't release
Dialogue: 0,00:08:47.44,00:08:48.96,Default,,0,0,0,,models which 1/10th the
Dialogue: 0,00:08:48.96,00:08:54.20,Default,,0,0,0,,price, then OpenAI and Anthropic
Dialogue: 0,00:08:54.20,00:08:56.40,Default,,0,0,0,,does not have any pressure here.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:56.40,00:08:58.68,Default,,0,0,0,,They've zero pressure to not increase the price.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:59.12,00:09:01.28,Default,,0,0,0,,So, then the 20$ subscription becomes
Dialogue: 0,00:09:01.28,00:09:02.36,Default,,0,0,0,,200$
Dialogue: 0,00:09:02.36,00:09:05.28,Default,,0,0,0,,And the 200$ subscription currently becaomes, let's say-
Dialogue: 0,00:09:05.28,00:09:07.40,Default,,0,0,0,,$10,000 Enterprise subscription
Dialogue: 0,00:09:07.40,00:09:09.56,Default,,0,0,0,,or something like that. So, this is
Dialogue: 0,00:09:09.56,00:09:10.84,Default,,0,0,0,,definitely useful.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:11.76,00:09:14.60,Default,,0,0,0,,But, the problems! The problems are because
Dialogue: 0,00:09:14.60,00:09:17.00,Default,,0,0,0,,as i said
Dialogue: 0,00:09:17.00,00:09:20.76,Default,,0,0,0,,The repos are public, the evaluations of public, and
Dialogue: 0,00:09:21.12,00:09:23.20,Default,,0,0,0,,the entire code patches,
Dialogue: 0,00:09:23.20,00:09:25.40,Default,,0,0,0,,everything is public. Like you can create
Dialogue: 0,00:09:25.40,00:09:27.84,Default,,0,0,0,,similar tasks that are in SWE Bench
Dialogue: 0,00:09:28.16,00:09:30.04,Default,,0,0,0,,and then you know match them to SWE Bench
Dialogue: 0,00:09:31.24,00:09:33.04,Default,,0,0,0,,you know like improve performance on SWE Bench.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:33.28,00:09:36.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Like, for example- let's say I have a Python repo, and it is
Dialogue: 0,00:09:36.96,00:09:39.92,Default,,0,0,0,,supposed to be some Django, REST API or something,
Dialogue: 0,00:09:39.92,00:09:43.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I can create something like, which also is a Django repo
Dialogue: 0,00:09:44.12,00:09:45.80,Default,,0,0,0,,But, it is doing -let's say- do list
Dialogue: 0,00:09:45.80,00:09:46.28,Default,,0,0,0,,or something
Dialogue: 0,00:09:46.28,00:09:48.24,Default,,0,0,0,,And if i train on
Dialogue: 0,00:09:48.24,00:09:50.44,Default,,0,0,0,,enough of these examples then I can improve
