Dialogue: 0,00:09:55.68,00:09:58.28,Default,,0,0,0,,A few months ago, the SWE Bench guys
Dialogue: 0,00:09:58.28,00:10:00.12,Default,,0,0,0,,released this, which is called: SWE Smith
Dialogue: 0,00:10:00.88,00:10:04.24,Default,,0,0,0,,This is interesting, because these guys
Dialogue: 0,00:10:04.24,00:10:06.84,Default,,0,0,0,,trained a 32B Model and
Dialogue: 0,00:10:06.92,00:10:09.44,Default,,0,0,0,,they were basically trying to scale the
Dialogue: 0,00:10:09.56,00:10:13.64,Default,,0,0,0,,amount of data for software engineering, and they used the same principles that I told you
Dialogue: 0,00:10:14.12,00:10:19.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, the performance here is 40.2% pass@1 on SWE Bench
Dialogue: 0,00:10:19.56,00:10:21.08,Default,,0,0,0,,which is right now like
